Original commit body from 31f151c8dfe58060a93c6fbfc1456c6e012f3dee:

An unresolved C/C++ call is stamped with every header its file can see
(INV-zikul / INV-valom), and that comma-joined list was the module slot:
part of the external symbol's id, its display label, the edge's dst and
its dst_ref, once per call site. On envoy a file sees ~140 headers, so
each of those strings ran 1-12 KB. envoy's survey was 5.5 GB, and
verify-claims was SIGKILLed at 20.5 GB when load_substrate re-read it.
envoy-half: 151,591 edges carried 2.07 GB of repeated lists against
14 MB of distinct content (3,657 lists, about one per file).

Owner ruling 2026-10-23: handle + side table. A slot naming two or more
modules is now `module-set-<16 hex>` (sha256 of the comma-joined list),
built by module_sets.module_slot in cpp.py and c.py. The list is stored
once in a new top-level `module_sets` table written by finalize.
survey_io.load_behavior_map registers it on every load, and refuses any
entry whose handle does not hash to its list. module_hint_disjuncts and
_module_hint_candidates, the two places the slot is split, expand the
handle first. So classification (ANY) and the coverage gate (ALL) read
the same list as before. A one-module slot is written as itself. A
handle with no table entry reads as one unenumerated module, which
withholds (fails closed), and warns once.

Versions (owner ruling: bump the stable_id scheme):
  SCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.15 -> 0.21.0. MINOR because a reader that split the
    slot on commas must now expand the handle first (spec: "Breaking
    output changes bump minor").
  stable_id_scheme v11 -> v12. The formula is unchanged, but its module
    path input is the handle for C/C++ externals with 2+ headers. No other
    value changes.

Measured A/B, pre-registered (lab notebook jahuf_10232026/; BEFORE = dev
88ac39f8a5, AFTER = this change):
  - Verdict envelopes identical on 8 of 8 repos with both arms: torsocks,
    modsecurity, whisper.cpp, sherpa-onnx, shaka-packager, plasma-desktop,
    grpc and envoy-half. Handles were expanded before comparing.
    whisper.cpp and sherpa-onnx differ only in the order of some
    sink_symbols lists (same strings, sorted by id).
  - Surveys identical on the same 8 after normalisation: masked hashes over
    dst strings, and order-insensitive lists.
  - Survey size: grpc 892 -> 495 MB, envoy-half 3,121 -> 490 MB.
  - Peak RSS: grpc 5.8 -> 4.4 GB, envoy-half 11.9 -> 3.7 GB.
  - Full envoy: dev is SIGKILLed at 20.3 GB; this change completes at
    6.0 GB with a 977 MB survey.

Stated limit: the handle bounds an id's size, not its dependence on
context. One external target still gets one node per distinct include
list (52,571 nodes for 12,160 names on envoy-half). Filed as INV-mujov.

Also: linkers/grpc.py's proto-service fold row became a named scalar
again. WI-fotad (6782e9bf28) turned `canonical_kind = "interface"` into the
tuple ("grpc_service", "interface"), and find_partial_abstract_family_literals
read the tuple as a partial interface/trait/protocol enumeration. That
failed test_no_language_agnostic_module_hand_rolls_a_partial_abstract_family
on dev; found here by the full suite.

